  "raw": {
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=35a5d7d3-e147-49ce-99d9-63ae0a4ffb39&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201864505399_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Theology and Philosophy, Visiting Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\n\nLocation: West Hartford\n\nAbout University of Saint Joseph   The University of Saint Joseph, founded by the Sisters of Mercy, provides a rigorous liberal arts and professional education for a diverse student population in an inclusive environment that encourages strong ethical values, personal integrity, and a sense of responsibility to the needs of society. The University has been recognized as a top national university in Connecticut by U.S. News & World Report's Best College Rankings including being the #1 Connecticut University in \"Top Performers on Social Mobility,\" #2 Connecticut University in \"Best Value Schools,\" and #3 Connecticut University in \"Best National Universities.\" Ideally situated midway between Boston and New York City, the beautiful 84-acre Olmsted-designed campus is one mile from West Hartford's thriving downtown, and provides an array of cultural events, occasions for spiritual development, and fitness and recreational options. The University also has an active presence outside our campus, reaching into the surrounding community through internships, community service projects, new programs and partnerships. At University of Saint Joseph, our mission statement profoundly resonates with our faculty and staff and serves as the foundation upon which our employment policy is built. We seek to attract, develop and retain individuals who are committed to our mission. We are committed to providing an environment where diverse talents, perspectives, experiences and contributions are recognized, and one that promotes the \"growth of the whole person\" with resources that enable employees to meet professional and personal life needs. Position Description The University of Saint Joseph invites applications for a full-time Visiting Assistant Professor of Theology and Philosophy to join a vibrant academic community committed to intellectual inquiry, excellent undergraduate teaching, and the formation of students as thoughtful, engaged members of society. We welcome scholars and teachers whose work engages theology, philosophy, religious studies, ethics, or related fields and who are excited to bring their expertise into conversation with a broad undergraduate curriculum. The successful candidate will teach introductory courses in Philosophy and Religious Studies, upper-level seminars, general education courses, and offerings connected to their scholarly interests. This position offers an opportunity to mentor and advise students, develop innovative courses and curricula, pursue scholarship and professional development, and participate actively in the intellectual and community life of the University. Candidates should have a strong understanding of the history of philosophy and an appreciation for the Catholic Intellectual Tradition and its significance for the mission and intellectual life of a Catholic university. Required Qualifications Candidates should have: Substantial competence in theology, philosophy, religious studies, or a closely related field. Demonstrated teaching experience and a commitment to undergraduate education. The ability to teach across a broad range of the department’s Philosophy and Religious Studies curriculum. Relevant scholarly expertise and a commitment to research and professional development. Preferred credentials: Preference will be given to candidates who hold, at the time of appointment, one of the following: An M.A. in Philosophy and a Ph.D. in Theology or Religious Studies; or An M.A. in Theology or Religious Studies and a Ph.D. in Philosophy. We also encourage applications from candidates with other relevant advanced degrees, interdisciplinary preparation, professional experience, or demonstrated expertise that would prepare them to contribute to the undergraduate curriculum. This is a full-time faculty position . The appointment may be renewed for an additional one-year visiting term and may, depending on institutional needs and performance, be considered for conversion to a tenure-track or non-tenure-track position after one or two years as a Visiting Assistant Professor. Join the University of Saint Joseph in creating an intellectually rich, student-centered learning environment where rigorous inquiry, meaningful mentorship, and the pursuit of wisdom thrive. Application Procedure Interested candidates should submit: Letter of interest addressing all qualifications for the position Current curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy and research interests (two pages maximum) Unofficial transcripts Three current professional references (contact information only) Terminal degree (PhD or ThD) in Theology, Religious Studies, or Philosophy by the appointment start date is required Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Preference will be given to applications received by 12/1/2026. The salary range for this position is within standard faculty compensation. Benefit eligible employees can participate in the University’s health and welfare benefits program, including medical/dental insurance, retirement plan (403b) matching, subject to the terms and eligibility requirements of the plan. Qualified employees may receive paid holidays, vacation time, sick time, paternity leave, tuition waiver, long-term disability and life insurance. Please visit our website to read more about our mission statement and learn more about our department and program",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=35a5d7d3-e147-49ce-99d9-63ae0a4ffb39&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201864418359_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Pharmacy Practice, Assistant Professor, NTT",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\n\nLocation: West Hartford\n\nAbout University of Saint Joseph   The University of Saint Joseph, founded by the Sisters of Mercy, provides a rigorous liberal arts and professional education for a diverse student population in an inclusive environment that encourages strong ethical values, personal integrity, and a sense of responsibility to the needs of society. The University has been recognized as a top national university in Connecticut by U.S. News & World Report's Best College Rankings including being the #1 Connecticut University in \"Top Performers on Social Mobility,\" #2 Connecticut University in \"Best Value Schools,\" and #3 Connecticut University in \"Best National Universities.\" Ideally situated midway between Boston and New York City, the beautiful 84-acre Olmsted-designed campus is one mile from West Hartford's thriving downtown, and provides an array of cultural events, occasions for spiritual development, and fitness and recreational options. The University also has an active presence outside our campus, reaching into the surrounding community through internships, community service projects, new program and partnerships. At University of Saint Joseph, our mission statement profoundly resonates with our faculty and staff and serves as the foundation upon which our employment policy is built. We seek to attract, develop and retain individuals who are committed to our mission. We are committed to providing an environment where diverse talents, perspectives, experiences and contributions are recognized, and one that promotes the \"growth of the whole person\" with resources that enable employees to meet professional and personal life needs. Position Description The University of Saint Joseph invites applications for a 12-month, non-tenure-track faculty position in the Department of Pharmacy Practice and Administration at the rank of Assistant Professor. We seek a pharmacist who is committed to teaching and mentoring Doctor of Pharmacy students and who will contribute to the School through scholarship and service appropriate to the appointment. The position may be structured as teaching-focused or include clinical practice responsibilities at an affiliated practice site, depending on the candidate’s background and the school’s needs. We are particularly seeking candidates with expertise in one or more of the following areas: Internal medicine, including psychiatry, respiratory disorders, infectious diseases, and gastrointestinal conditions Community pharmacy Pharmacy administration, health systems practice, or pharmacy law and policy Candidates do not need experience in every area listed. We welcome applicants from different practice settings who can bring their expertise to the PharmD curriculum. Responsibilities include (but are not limited to): Development and delivery of high-quality didactic, lab and/or experiential pharmacy courses Engagement in scholarly research activities, publications, and presentations Mentorship and advisement to pharmacy students Participation in departmental and university service activities Collaboration with interdisciplinary teams to enhance pharmacy education and practice Requirements Doctor of Pharmacy degree (PharmD) from an accredited institution  Licensure/eligibility for licensure, in the State of Connecticut Completion of a residency program (PGY1 and/or PGY2) or equivalent experience Demonstrated potential for scholarly research and publications Excellent communication, interpersonal, and leadership skills Preferred Qualifications Board certification in a pharmacy specialty Prior teaching experience in an academic setting Experience with innovative teaching methodologies and technology-enhanced learning The successful candidate will support the School’s mission by delivering high-quality teaching in the Doctor of Pharmacy curriculum, contributing to curriculum development and assessment, and mentoring students. Candidates with clinical training may maintain a practice site and serve as preceptors for pharmacy students. Faculty are encouraged to engage in scholarship and service activities aligned with their expertise and institutional goals. Application Instructions Persons interested please submit:  Current Curriculum Vitae Cover letter, including description of pharmacy related interests and salary expectations Teaching philosophy (two pages maximum) Three current professional references (contact information only) Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Preference will be given to applications received by 11/15/2026. Please visit our website to read more about our mission statement and learn more about our department and program.  The salary range for this position falls within the standard Faculty compensation.  Benefit eligible employees can participate in the University’s health and welfare benefits program, including medical/dental insurance, retirement plan (403b) matching, subject to the terms and eligibility requirements of the plan. Qualified employees may receive paid holidays, vacation time, sick time, paternity leave, tuition waiver, long-term disability and life insurance.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=35a5d7d3-e147-49ce-99d9-63ae0a4ffb39&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200695477224_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Nursing, Clinical Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\n\nLocation: Hartford\n\nThank you for considering University of Saint Joseph in your search. About University of Saint Joseph: The University of Saint Joseph, founded by the Sisters of Mercy, provides a rigorous liberal arts and professional education for a diverse student population in an inclusive environment that encourages strong ethical values, personal integrity, and a sense of responsibility to the needs of society. The University has been recognized as a top national university in Connecticut by U.S. News & World Report's Best College Rankings including being the #1 Connecticut University in \"Top Performers on Social Mobility,\" #2 Connecticut University in \"Best Value Schools,\" and #3 Connecticut University in \"Best National Universities.\" Ideally situated midway between Boston and New York City, the beautiful 90-acre Olmsted-designed campus is one mile from West Hartford's thriving downtown, and provides an array of cultural events, occasions for spiritual development, and fitness and recreational options. The University also has an active presence outside our campus, reaching into the surrounding community through internships, community service projects, new program and partnerships. At University of Saint Joseph, our mission statement profoundly resonates with our faculty and staff and serves as the foundation upon which our employment policy is built. We seek to attract, develop and retain individuals who are committed to our mission. We are committed to providing an environment where diverse talents, perspectives, experiences and contributions are recognized, and one that promotes the \"growth of the whole person\" with resources that enable employees to meet professional and personal life needs. Job Description: The University of Saint Joseph invites qualified applicants to serve as adjunct faculty within the Nursing Department.  The department is actively recruiting several adjuncts for the Fall  semester for faculty to teach in all clinical Undergraduate Nursing Courses. Responsibilities include (but are not limited to): Teach students at assigned clinical sites. Grade all student assignments in a timely manner. Provide appropriate feedback to students to promote academic success. Attend program/department meetings as requested. Demonstrate knowledge of the current methods and practices for teaching college-level courses; present qualified and clear instruction related to the course subject. Learn and utilize technology offered at USJ to facilitate teaching. Meet all designated class periods in the semester as dictated by the academic calendar. Submit mid-semester and final grades to the Registrar's Office within required time-frames, leave all course records with the department chairperson upon completion of the course. Provide a supportive atmosphere for student success. Requirements: Master's degree or higher in the scientific discipline of Nursing or related field when teaching undergraduate courses. Degrees must be from a regionally accredited institution. Prior teaching experience strongly preferred. Commitment to the mission of the University of Saint Joseph Physical ability to perform essential functions of the position, with or without reasonable accommodation. Additional Information: Teaching assignments are on a semester basis only and are dependent on student enrollment and department need. Clinicals are offered at various times, including day, evening, weekdays, and Saturdays. Please indicate in your cover letter your general availability and your experience teaching in various formats. Regular attendance is an essential job function as it demonstrates dependability towards the performance of job duties.  Application Instructions: Persons interested in the above position should apply online.  Please submit: Resume/Curriculum Vitale The Department Chairperson will review your application. If there is an opening in a subject area you are qualified to teach, the department will contact you directly to discuss the specific opportunity. Thank you for your interest in joining the University of Saint Joseph as adjunct faculty.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=35a5d7d3-e147-49ce-99d9-63ae0a4ffb39&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201861891119_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Physician Asst. Studies/Health Science, Asst./Assoc. Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\n\nLocation: West Hartford\n\nAbout University of Saint Joseph   The University of Saint Joseph, founded by the Sisters of Mercy, provides a rigorous liberal arts and professional education for a diverse student population in an inclusive environment that encourages strong ethical values, personal integrity, and a sense of responsibility to the needs of society. The University has been recognized as a top national university in Connecticut by U.S. News & World Report's Best College Rankings including being the #1 Connecticut University in \"Top Performers on Social Mobility,\" #2 Connecticut University in \"Best Value Schools,\" and #3 Connecticut University in \"Best National Universities.\" Ideally situated midway between Boston and New York City, the beautiful 84-acre Olmsted-designed campus is one mile from West Hartford's thriving downtown, and provides an array of cultural events, occasions for spiritual development, and fitness and recreational options. The University also has an active presence outside our campus, reaching into the surrounding community through internships, community service projects, new program and partnerships. At University of Saint Joseph, our mission statement profoundly resonates with our faculty and staff and serves as the foundation upon which our employment policy is built. We seek to attract, develop and retain individuals who are committed to our mission. We are committed to providing an environment where diverse talents, perspectives, experiences and contributions are recognized, and one that promotes the \"growth of the whole person\" with resources that enable employees to meet professional and personal life needs. Position Description The Department of Physician Assistant Studies and Department of Nutrition and Public Health at the University of Saint Joseph invite applications for a joint, full-time, 12-month non-tenure-track faculty position in PA studies/health science at the rank of Assistant Professor or Associate Professor starting in January 2027 or August 2027. The rank will be determined based on the academic and professional qualifications and experiences of the candidate.  Candidates are expected to demonstrate potential for excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. The position is a joint faculty appointment between the PA Studies program and the Health Science program. Responsibilities include curriculum development, teaching, assessment, and remediation in both undergraduate and graduate courses as well as student advising. Additional responsibilities include participation in PAS and NUPH department/program meetings, PA Studies admissions, continuous program-analysis, and other responsibilities as assigned. The ideal candidate will have both teaching and clinical experience and use evidence-based best practices in support of the education of health science professionals through an interdisciplinary lens.  Required Skills/Qualifications Graduate of a physician assistant program accredited by the Accreditation Review Commission on Education for the Physician Assistant (ARC-PA) Terminal degree for discipline, with a minimum of a Master’s National Commission on Certification of Physician Assistants (NCCPA) certified Active, unencumbered state physician assistant license 2 years of clinical practice in a licensed discipline preferred Higher education experience preferred Strong communication, time management and organizational skills Demonstrated ability to work as a member of a team of highly motivated and experienced individuals Honesty, integrity, and commitment to maintaining high professional standards Commitment to the mission and values of the University and to the highest standards of the profession Developing or continuing an active program of scholarship preferred Application Procedure Interested candidates should submit:  Letter of interest addressing all qualifications for the position Current curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy and research interests (two pages maximum)  Unofficial transcripts Three current professional references with addresses (contact information only) Please visit our website to read more about our mission statement and learn more about our department and program.  The salary range for this position falls within the standard Faculty compensation.  Benefit eligible employees can participate in the University’s health and welfare benefits program, including medical/dental insurance, retirement plan (403b) matching, subject to the terms and eligibility requirements of the plan. Qualified employees may receive paid holidays, vacation time, sick time, paternity leave, tuition waiver, long-term disability and life insurance.",
