    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=35a5d7d3-e147-49ce-99d9-63ae0a4ffb39&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200985514605_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Senior Leadership Gifts Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\n\nLocation: West Hartford\n\nReporting to the Vice President of Institutional Advancement, this individual is responsible for working independently to manage a portfolio of prospects and donors and grow financial support for USJ. A successful Senior Leadership Gift Officer will proactively develop appropriate cultivation, solicitation and stewardship strategies and lead moves management program to build on-going relationships within the donor community. This individual will remain focused on the identification, cultivation and solicitation of individuals, corporations and foundations to support all areas of the University. Portfolio Management: Identify, qualify, cultivate, solicit and steward an active portfolio of 100 to 150 prospective and current donors, moving through the stewardship cycle. Donor Engagement: Conduct appropriate and consistent contact, making regular face-to-face or virtual visits annually to build trust-based relationships and match donor passions with USJ priorities.  Direct Solicitation: Lead gift discussions, prepare proposals, draft gift agreements, and close major financial commitments. Cross-Functional Collaboration: Partner with board members, institutional leaders, and faculty experts to develop opportunities; and provide support of USJ targeted initiatives. Metrics & Tracking: Use Raiser Edge databases to gather, record and properly store information along with tracking tools to forecast revenue, and meet performance goals. Other responsibilities as assigned. DECISION MAKING Manage time to initiate on and off campus prospect visits Match institutional funding priorities to donor interests Craft persuasive solicitations that result in gifts for the University Education & Experience Bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience required. Ten+ years fundraising experience in higher education or relevant alternate experience strongly preferred Other Qualifications Strong analytical skills, organizational skills and attention to detail Excellent oral and written skills and ability to communicate comfortably with external constituents, colleagues and students Exhibits a high level of professionalism, leadership, creative problem solving, diplomacy, negotiation and sales skills, and the ability to manage complex projects with minimal supervision Demonstrated ability to establish and build relationships with individual donors, corporations and foundations and to understand the needs and interests of donors; willingness to travel extensively and work evenings and weekends as necessary Strong personal and professional integrity; must handle confidential information and materials with discretion Excellent computer skills; proficiency with MS Office Suite with strong working abilities in Microsoft Word and Excel, ability to utilize technological resources to maximum advantage. Experience with Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge strongly preferred Flexible and able to multi-task Able to function independently while operating effectively within a team environment Ability and willingness to travel and work occasional evenings and weekends Enthusiastic belief in the mission, core values and future of the University of Saint Joseph Physical ability to perform essential functions of the position, with or without reasonable accommodation",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=35a5d7d3-e147-49ce-99d9-63ae0a4ffb39&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201860584050_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Nursing, Assistant/Associate Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\n\nLocation: West Hartford\n\nAbout University of Saint Joseph   The University of Saint Joseph, founded by the Sisters of Mercy, provides a rigorous liberal arts and professional education for a diverse student population in an inclusive environment that encourages strong ethical values, personal integrity, and a sense of responsibility to the needs of society. The University has been recognized as a top national university in Connecticut by U.S. News & World Report's Best College Rankings including being the #1 Connecticut University in \"Top Performers on Social Mobility,\" #2 Connecticut University in \"Best Value Schools,\" and #3 Connecticut University in \"Best National Universities.\" Ideally situated midway between Boston and New York City, the beautiful 84-acre Olmsted-designed campus is one mile from West Hartford's thriving downtown, and provides an array of cultural events, occasions for spiritual development, and fitness and recreational options. The University also has an active presence outside our campus, reaching into the surrounding community through internships, community service projects, new program and partnerships. At University of Saint Joseph, our mission statement profoundly resonates with our faculty and staff and serves as the foundation upon which our employment policy is built. We seek to attract, develop and retain individuals who are committed to our mission. We are committed to providing an environment where diverse talents, perspectives, experiences and contributions are recognized, and one that promotes the \"growth of the whole person\" with resources that enable employees to meet professional and personal life needs. Position Description The University of Saint Joseph invites applications for a dynamic leader to serve as Director of Graduate Nursing Programs. This is an exciting opportunity to provide leadership, academic oversight, and operational direction across our range of programs including Master’s (with FNP or PMHNP specialization), Doctoral (DNP), and Post-Graduate Certificate programs. This full-time, 12-month, Tenure Track/ Non-Tenure Track position includes the opportunity to collaborate with and mentor faculty and directly engage with students through teaching and advising. The ideal candidate will use evidence-based best practices in nursing education and cultivate robust clinical partnerships to optimize the practice-readiness of advanced practice nurses and leaders. The ideal candidate should demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in teaching, continued professional development, have a record of service to the School/University, and work collaboratively with colleagues in the department and across the university. Responsibilities: Oversee curriculum development and continuous improvements in collaboration with track coordinators, to align with accreditation standards, industry needs, and best practices in advanced nursing education. Collaborate with clinical partners to secure and maintain high-quality clinical placements that support student learning and program objectives. Engage in ongoing program evaluation and accreditation activities, including data collection, analysis, and reporting. Contribute to strategic initiatives related to program marketing, student recruitment, and enrollment growth. Deliver high-quality instruction and mentorship to graduate students, foster clinical competence, professional growth, and evidence-based practice. Provide advising, mentorship, and professional guidance to graduate students, supporting their academic success, clinical competence, and transition into advanced nursing practice. Maintain active engagement in professional organizations and networks to enhance program visibility and ensure alignment with current trends in advanced practice nursing. Collaborate across departments and disciplines to support interprofessional education and community engagement initiatives. Required Qualifications Doctoral degree in nursing or a related field (PhD, EdD, DNP) Licensed or eligible for license by the state of Connecticut as a Registered Nurse Minimum of five years of clinical practice experience. Minimum of three years of full-time experience in teaching and curriculum development at the collegiate level. Commitment to the mission and values of the University and to the highest standards of the profession of Nursing. Preferred Qualifications Leadership experience in higher education Experience in online education Licensed or eligible for license by the state of Connecticut as an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse. Developing or continuing an active program of scholarship. Application Procedure Interested candidates should submit:  Letter of interest addressing all qualifications for the position Current curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy and research interests (two pages maximum)  Unofficial transcripts Three current professional references (contact information only) Please visit our website to read more about our mission statement and learn more about our department and program.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=35a5d7d3-e147-49ce-99d9-63ae0a4ffb39&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200963035674_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "LPN/Teachers Asst One-to-One, Gengras Center School",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\n\nLocation: West Hartford\n\nThank you for considering University of Saint Joseph in your search. About University of Saint Joseph: The Gengras Center School, founded in 1965 on the campus of University of Saint Joseph, provides a unique program for elementary, middle, high school and transition aged students with significant intellectual and developmental disabilities, autism and related behavioral challenges. Our state-approved, private special education school offers highly structured, functional, self-contained programs for over 130 students. Our staff-to-student ratio is higher than average, and the collaboration between families, home school districts, and community-based service providers is incomparable. Surrounded by Georgian architecture, spacious walking paths and the eager faces of University of Saint Joseph's young scholars, Gengras Center students and staff members have an added sense of purpose and confidence simply by being part of this University campus environment and all the marvelous facilities that are part of it. Staff enjoy a 10-month schedule working traditional school hours, time off during school vacations, and receive additional pay for working summer school during July. The university offers benefits to all full-time employees, including medical, dental, retirement, and a generous tuition waiver program for those seeking to continue their education. More information about the Gengras Center can be found at  https://www.gengrascenter.org/  Job Description: This position supports the Gengras Center by providing health services, medical treatment and skilled nursing care as prescribed for students with special health care needs.    Working under the direct supervision of the professional staff, this position supports the Gengras Center by providing instructional assistance within the classroom to individuals, and small and large groups, providing clerical and organizational assistance for classroom teachers and/or the school nurse, and by providing general supervision and management of the students.  This position will assist the school nurse in carrying out selected activities related to assigned students and/or the school health program.  The nurse will assist classroom staff and parents with student health care issues, and will provide training and instruction on related health topics.  Maintaining pertinent health records, IEP’s and mandated individual health care forms according to state requirements is also necessary.  This position must also coordinate health services and implement health policies and procedures with the Center’s nurse and administration. Responsibilities (include but are not limited to): Assist school nurse in carrying out selected clinically-based activities related to students and student health care programs. Prepare and maintain health room and therapy areas. Assist the school nurse with health screenings, health assessment procedures and individual health care plans. Perform routine clerical duties in the health office required, such as: recording standardized information on cumulative health records, assisting with telephone communications, inventory and requisition of supplies, assisting in data collection, and filing and typing. Provide routine nursing care of students, as directed. Administer medication. Perform and assist the nurse with first-aid procedures, as directed. Assist the school nurse with acute medical emergencies, as directed. Monitor and care for students (Taking vital signs and monitoring body temperature, administering J and G tube feedings, toileting support, child hygiene, transferring students, etc.). Demonstrate an awareness of the Center's medical policies/procedures. Support the instructional process/program and classroom teacher. Assist professionals with building and maintaining effective instructional teams. Attend transdisciplinary team meetings and actively participating in the process. Assist professionals with maintaining learner-centered, supportive environments. Assist professionals with planning and organizing learning experiences. Assist with the development/preparation of learning materials/instructional resources and the environment. Assist with direct instruction and learner needs, progress, and achievements. Perform clerical duties in the classroom, such as record keeping, data entry, assisting with parent communication (phone, email, communication books), inventory/requisition of supplies and materials, and typing or filing. Demonstrate effective utilization of behavior management procedures in supervision of assigned students. Supervise students for school related activities as assigned, including participating in community outings/worksites and extracurricular activities. Support The Gengras Center as a school and as a program: Provide substitute coverage, within the scope of practices outlined above, in the absence of the RN. Participate in all in-service and program development workshops, and continue to grow professionally. Participate actively on school committees. Demonstrate knowledge of the Center’s policies/procedures.  Perform other duties assigned by the Director, Assistant Director, teachers or related services staff, as indicated within the Gengras Center’s development plan, or as required by the student’s Individualized Education Plan and Individualized Health Care Plans.  Requirements: Licensed Practical Nurse Degree. Previous experience in working with children preferred. Demonstrate skills in flexibility, confidentiality and sound decision making. Availability to work during the summer program, as needed. Physical ability to perform the essential functions of the position, with or without reasonable accommodation.  Application Instructions: Persons interested in the above position should apply online.  Please submit:   Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover letter with salary requirements Professional references",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=35a5d7d3-e147-49ce-99d9-63ae0a4ffb39&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201860432233_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Clinical Psychology, Assistant/Associate Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\n\nLocation: West Hartford\n\nAbout University of Saint Joseph   The University of Saint Joseph, founded by the Sisters of Mercy, provides a rigorous liberal arts and professional education for a diverse student population in an inclusive environment that encourages strong ethical values, personal integrity, and a sense of responsibility to the needs of society. The University has been recognized as a top national university in Connecticut by U.S. News & World Report's Best College Rankings including being the #1 Connecticut University in \"Top Performers on Social Mobility,\" #2 Connecticut University in \"Best Value Schools,\" and #3 Connecticut University in \"Best National Universities.\" Ideally situated midway between Boston and New York City, the beautiful 84-acre Olmsted-designed campus is one mile from West Hartford's thriving downtown, and provides an array of cultural events, occasions for spiritual development, and fitness and recreational options. The University also has an active presence outside our campus, reaching into the surrounding community through internships, community service projects, new program and partnerships. At University of Saint Joseph, our mission statement profoundly resonates with our faculty and staff and serves as the foundation upon which our employment policy is built. We seek to attract, develop and retain individuals who are committed to our mission. We are committed to providing an environment where diverse talents, perspectives, experiences and contributions are recognized, and one that promotes the \"growth of the whole person\" with resources that enable employees to meet professional and personal life needs. Position Description The University invites applications for a full time (9 month) faculty position with a focus on Clinical Psychology in the Psychology program. The position may be tenure-track or not tenure-track. The Psychology program is in a vibrant and collegial department that also includes programs in Criminal and Restorative Justice and Child Study. The department prides itself on student-centered excellence in undergraduate teaching and its supportive culture. The Psychology program offers an undergraduate bachelor’s degree in Psychology, a minor in Psychology, an accelerated pathway to the MA in Counseling, a Child Life Specialist track, and concentrations and certificates in Criminal Justice/Mental Health, Behavioral Analysis, and Expressive Therapies. The position is scheduled to begin in August 2027. Preference will be given to applicants with a demonstrated commitment to student-centered teaching. Candidate should possess expertise in Clinical Psychology, Counseling Psychology, or Mental Health Counseling. This position is an exciting opportunity for candidates who want to use their clinical expertise to mentor undergraduate students who are potentially interested in pursuing careers in mental health in a highly collaborative and interdisciplinary setting. The program emphasizes small classes and close working relationships between students and faculty and takes pride in preparing undergraduate students for a wide range of professional fields.  The successful candidate will be able to teach undergraduate courses in Psychopathology and Internship   seminar, as well as other courses in their areas of expertise. Examples of possible additional courses to be taught include Introductory Psychology, courses at the intersection of Criminal and Restorative Justice and Psychology, courses in Expressive Therapies, and courses in human development. If the successful candidate is hired on the tenure-track, they will teach 12 credits per semester at the undergraduate level, engage in scholarship, and participate in service to the department, university, and community. If the position is not tenure-track, the successful candidate will teach 12 credits per semester at the undergraduate level, participate in service to the department, university, and community, and has the option to maintain clinical practice hours   outside of the university.    Required Skills/Qualifications Minimum requirements:  Master’s degree in Psychology, Counseling, or closely related field. Prior experience providing direct client care in a clinical, community or private practice setting. Must hold or have previously held a valid state license as a clinical psychologist, LPC, or equivalent mental health credential.  Demonstrated excellence in teaching and mentoring undergraduate students or evidence of strong potential in these areas. Preferred: Terminal degree (PhD or PsyD) in Clinical or Counseling Psychology For a tenure-track position, a terminal degree (PhD or PsyD) in Clinical or Counseling Psychology and a demonstrated record of a program of scholarship is required.  Application Procedure Interested candidates should submit:  Letter of interest addressing all qualifications for the position Current curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy and research interests (two pages maximum)  Unofficial transcripts Three current professional references (contact information only) Terminal degree (PhD or PsyD) in Clinical or Counseling Psychology by the appointment start date is required Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Preference will be given to applications received by 11/6/2026. Please visit our website to read more about our mission statement and learn more about our department and program.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=35a5d7d3-e147-49ce-99d9-63ae0a4ffb39&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201854698999_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Coordinator of Graduate Programs for Teachers",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-10\n\nLocation: West Hartford\n\nThe Coordinator of Graduate Programs for Teachers supports the implementation, coordination, and daily operation of graduate programs serving in service teachers within the Department of Education. Reporting to the Associate Director of Teacher Education Programs, this position is responsible for managing program logistics, scheduling, student workflow processes, data collection, and instructional systems. The Coordinator works closely with the Associate Director, Department Chair, Faculty Advisors, and administrative staff to ensure the efficient delivery of cohort-based graduate programs. This role supports program assessment, accreditation, and continuous improvement processes through coordination of data, documentation, and reporting systems. Program Coordination and Operations Coordinate the day-to-day operations of graduate programs for practicing teachers. Manage cohort schedules, including course sequencing, timelines, and program progression. Coordinate and support cohort orientation sessions, including recording and distribution of virtual orientation materials. Complete first-class attendance verification and compliance processes at the start of each academic term. Maintain program calendars, timelines, and operational tracking systems. Coordinate implementation of integrated programs of study in consultation with department administration to support student progression. Serve as the primary liaison with K-12 Teachers Alliance (KTA) partners, coordinating cohort operations, partner communications, and activities that support educator recruitment, enrollment, and program success. Scheduling, Enrollment, and Faculty Coordination Develop and maintain course schedules in coordination with the Associate Director and Department Chair. Coordinate course scheduling logistics to ensure alignment with program requirements and faculty availability. Work with the Associate Director to identify adjunct faculty needs based on enrollment and scheduling demands. Support registration processes and coordinate with the Registrar’s Office regarding enrollment and course-related issues. Monitor enrollment and assist with adjustments to course sections as needed. Student Support and Program Processes Coordinate the logistics of student onboarding and orientation in collaboration with faculty advisors and administrative staff. Support faculty advisors in developing and revising student plans of study by maintaining documentation and tracking progression. Collaborate with faculty advisors and department leadership to support student success by identifying operational needs and facilitating resolution of program-related issues. Maintain program-level communication materials and workflows to ensure timely and accurate dissemination of information. Coordinate with the Coordinator of Clinical Placement to support practicum and cross-endorsement placement processes. Collaborate with the Administrative and Student Support Assistant to design and monitor individualized student programs, monitor schedule adjustments, and resolve integrated cohort challenges. Curriculum Materials and Records Management Maintain up-to-date records of course syllabi, textbooks, instructional materials, and program calendars. Ensure alignment among course documentation, Learning Management System (LMS) content, and program requirements. Organize and maintain program files and records in accordance with departmental and accreditation requirements. Learning Management System and Instructional Support Maintain and manage the LMS (Blackboard) for online graduate programs courses. Coordinate with faculty and adjuncts to update and maintain course shells. Ensure consistency in course organization and structure across program offerings. Set up and maintain gradebooks in alignment with course syllabi and requirements. Provide basic technical support and guidance to adjunct faculty regarding LMS use. Assessment, Surveys, and Data Support Coordinate and support the organization and review of capstone projects. Administer candidate surveys, including program entry, mid-program, and end-of-program evaluations. Collect, organize, and maintain program data related to student performance, satisfaction, and outcomes. Provide data collection and reporting support for program reviews and continuous improvement processes. Accreditation and Compliance Support Maintain documentation and data systems required for program review and accreditation. Assist in preparing materials and reports for accreditation and compliance processes. Track program data, student progression, and required documentation to ensure compliance with institutional and regulatory standards. Program Development Support Provide operational support for new program development and approval processes. Coordinate logistics for new program implementation, including scheduling, systems setup, and communication processes. Collaborate with internal offices (Registrar, IT, Enrollment Management) to support program operations. Administrative Coordination Coordinate communication across faculty, staff, and administrative offices to support program delivery. Maintain accurate and organized program records and files. Support planning and coordination of program-related meetings and events. Work collaboratively with the Administrative and Student Support Assistant to ensure effective execution of logistics and communications.  Education & Certification Master’s degree in Education or related field required Valid teaching certification Experience Experience in PK-12 experience or program coordination in higher ed required Experience with graduate or cohort-based programs preferred  Experience with learning management systems (e.g., Blackboard) preferred Connecticut 092 preferred Other Qualifications Demonstrated ability to work collegially, balance and prioritize assignments, and manage multiple projects Strong organizational, interpersonal, and customer service skills; ability to manage changing priorities and meet deadlines Excellent oral and written skills and ability to communicate comfortably with students, colleagues, and external constituents  Possess solid general computer skills, including ability to work in a Windows environment.  Demonstrated ability to recognize and appropriately handle matters of a confidential nature  Professional, courteous demeanor and appearance; ability to work professionally with students, faculty, staff and administration and represent the University professionally to the public Commitment to the mission of the University of Saint Joseph Physical ability to perform essential functions of the position, with or without reasonable accommodation",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=35a5d7d3-e147-49ce-99d9-63ae0a4ffb39&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201853857147_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant, School of Pharmacy/PA Studies",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\n\nLocation: West Hartford\n\nThe position supports the operations of the School of Pharmacy and Physician Assistant Studies. This position will be assigned tasks by the dean, but a primary responsibility is for administrative, operational, and logistical functions supporting experiential education and admissions for both school programs. The position serves as a liaison between the school, clinical affiliates, and the university community by interacting with students, faculty, staff, preceptors, and administration. The position also supports Pharmacy and PA admissions through application review, as well as prepping for and participating in interview days and open houses. Strong communication and relational skills, as well as organizational and technical abilities are required in order to perform this job successfully.  Schedule appointments and coordinate arrangements for meetings, conferences, and travel. Coordinate and verify completion of student and preceptor requirements for the Pharmacy Program.  Respond to routine requests for information regarding all School programs and events and refer complex requests to appropriate staff or faculty members. Provide support to students, preceptors, and pharmacy department for experiential learning management systems  Assist in daily functioning of the school, including supplies, mailings (including bulk), filing of sensitive data, student records upkeep and other file management. Assist in coordinating logistics for School events such as orientations, white coat ceremonies, hooding ceremonies, interview days, and open houses. Collect and disseminate information within and beyond the University accordingly. Organize and maintain the pharmacy program’s Experiential Learning Management System, computer files, office files, and records in accordance with School procedures, and follow up on pending matters.  Uses appropriate technology to compose and produce professional correspondence, minutes of meetings, presentations, spreadsheets, databases, and reports. Disseminate information accordingly. Recognize and maintain circumstances of a confidential nature. Perform other related duties as required. Assist Pharmacy’s Director of Experiential Education with establishment, coordination, and maintenance of clinical sites, placements, and preceptors for pharmacy student experiences. Function as school liaison between the university, preceptors, and clinical site representatives. Assist in reviewing affiliates’ organizational structure to ensure student compliance with requirements of each affiliate, preparing and ensuring of delivery of information to clinical sites in a timely and accurate manner. Assist the Assistant Dean of Admissions & Student Experience with application review. Prepare for interview days including but not limited to printing materials, stuffing folders, arranging classroom furniture; assist in interview day sessions as needed. Education & Experience High School diploma or equivalent required; Bachelors’ degree strongly preferred. Other Qualifications Two to three years’ administrative assistant experience preferred One to two years’ experience in a health care or educational setting or recruiting/staffing experience, or equivalent education and experience preferred Strong project management and analytical skills; strong organizational skills and attention to detail Able to function independently while operating effectively within a team environment Possess solid general computer skills, including ability to work in a Windows environment. Familiarity with specific applications used by the University/Department a plus Excellent oral and written skills and ability to communicate comfortably with students, colleagues, and external constituents Demonstrated ability to handle complex and multiple tasks in a professional and efficient manner Demonstrated ability to recognize and appropriately handle matters of a confidential nature  Exhibits a high level of professionalism, creative problem solving, diplomacy, and the ability to manage complex projects with minimal supervision Professional, courteous demeanor and appearance; ability to engage positively and work professionally with students, faculty, staff and administration and represent the University professionally in diverse clinical settings Commitment to the mission of the University of Saint Joseph Physical ability to perform essential functions of the position, with or without reasonable accommodation",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=35a5d7d3-e147-49ce-99d9-63ae0a4ffb39&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201853674663_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Cashier/Accounting Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\n\nLocation: West Hartford\n\nUnder the direction of the Assistant Controller, the Cashier/Accounting Specialist III performs a variety of accounting tasks both routine and project related. The responsibilities include those of the head cashier, daily cash management reporting, a variety of monthly reconciliations. Project related responsibilities are essential to gathering, classification and reporting of the University’s financial data. Receives cash and checks from students, logs receipt. Serves as point person for online payment systems.  Performs balance sheet reconciliations monthly, prior to monthly closing; researches and resolves variances. Performs review roles in Accounts Payable and Student Refund processes. Supports Campus Card, P-Card , and accounts payable operations. Supports the year-end closing and audit. Works collaboratively with the finance team to improve accounting procedures/controls, and efficiencies thru development and implementation. Communicates with the University community and outside vendors in support of payable operations. Performs other duties as assigned. Ensures appropriate internal controls are established and maintained. Performs work under the direction of the Assistant Controller. Education & Experience Associate’s degree in accounting preferred 2+ years related experience preferred Experience in non-profit environment – Jenzabar System experience preferred. Other Qualifications Strong analytical and organizational skills and attention to detail. Able to function independently while operating effectively within a team environment Possess solid general computer skills, including ability to work in a Windows environment. Proficiency with MS Office Suite, Internet, and other programs as needed. Familiarity with specific applications used by the University/Department a plus. Demonstrated ability to work collegially, balance and prioritize assignments, manage multiple projects, problem solve and offer secretarial support to more than one person Flexible and able to multi-task Demonstrated excellent oral and written communication skills Professional, courteous demeanor and appearance; ability to work professionally with students, faculty, staff and administration and represent the University professionally to the public Physical ability to perform essential functions of the position, with or without reasonable accommodation.",
      "department": ""
    },
