    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=35a5d7d3-e147-49ce-99d9-63ae0a4ffb39&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200971762499_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Tennis, Assistant Men's and Women's Coach",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-24\n\nLocation: West Hartford\n\nResponsibilities include assisting the head coach with the organizing and directing all aspects of a successful and competitive collegiate program. The recruitment of qualified student-athletes and a demonstrated commitment to their personal, athletic, and academic success are essential. Responsibilities may also include recruiting, travel management, scheduling, player development, and budget management. This is a part-time appointment. Assist in the process of recruiting prospective qualified student-athletes. Assist in the development and supervision of practice and game planning.   Assist with the orga nization of team travel.  Effectively demonstrates technical skills at the collegiate level Assist with fundraising. Ensure compliance with all College, NCAA Division III and CNE policies and procedures. Performs other related duties as required by the Head Men's and Women’s Tennis Coach Education & Experience Bachelor’s Degree preferred Previous coaching experience at the secondary and/or college level preferred Other Qualifications Physical ability to perform essential functions of the position, as noted below, with or without reasonable accommodation Physical Requirements The physical requirements and description of the work environment are representative of what an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable  accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Physical Activity Approximate Percentage of Time Spent in this Activity (Minimal, Some, Substantial) Bending Substantial Climbing (e.g. stairs) Substantial Keyboarding Substantial Kneeling Substantial Lifting (indicate maximum weight) Substantial Reaching Substantial Sitting Substantial Standing Substantial Using Telephone Substantial Walking Substantial Other (please explain): Substantial Work Environment (a brief description) The Athletic Department is a fast paced, intensive, high energy environment. Coaches and Staff work intensive schedules including weekends and evenings.",
